Follow-up on the default schema resolution in FrameworkBundle.

I extended `resolveDefaultSchema()` to cover more well-known config files, matching the JSON Schema Store catalog conventions:
- `config/routes.yaml` and `config/routes/**/*.yaml` -> routing schema
- `config/services.yaml` and `config/services_*.yaml` -> services schema
- `config/serializer/**/*.yaml` -> serialization schema (only when the Serializer component is installed)
- `config/validator/**/*.yaml` -> validation schema (only when the Validator component is installed)

Two related changes:
- The routing pattern now uses `config/routes` (Flex convention) instead of `config/routing`.
- The generated `config/schema.json` fallback is now limited to `config/packages/**/*.yaml`, since it only describes bundle configuration. Any other file has no default schema.

I also dropped the dead `class_exists(Route::class)` guard (code and test), as routing is a hard dependency of FrameworkBundle.

Tests use a `#[DataProvider]` for the four component schemas, plus cases for the `config/packages` fallback and for files outside it.

